{
  "id": "prob.bayes.tree",
  "title": "Bayes as a probability tree",
  "viewBox": [0, 0, 360, 260],
  "objects": [
    {"id": "root", "kind": "node", "x": 36, "y": 130, "r": 24, "label": "Start"},
    {"id": "D", "kind": "node", "x": 140, "y": 70, "label": "D"},
    {"id": "N", "kind": "node", "x": 140, "y": 190, "label": "not D"},
    {"id": "e1", "kind": "edge", "from": "root", "to": "D", "label": "0.01"},
    {"id": "e2", "kind": "edge", "from": "root", "to": "N", "label": "0.99"},
    {"id": "Dp", "kind": "node", "x": 250, "y": 40, "r": 17, "label": "+"},
    {"id": "Dn", "kind": "node", "x": 250, "y": 100, "r": 17, "label": "-"},
    {"id": "Np", "kind": "node", "x": 250, "y": 160, "r": 17, "label": "+"},
    {"id": "Nn", "kind": "node", "x": 250, "y": 220, "r": 17, "label": "-"},
    {"id": "e3", "kind": "edge", "from": "D", "to": "Dp", "label": "0.95"},
    {"id": "e4", "kind": "edge", "from": "D", "to": "Dn", "label": "0.05"},
    {"id": "e5", "kind": "edge", "from": "N", "to": "Np", "label": "0.05"},
    {"id": "e6", "kind": "edge", "from": "N", "to": "Nn", "label": "0.95"},
    {"id": "p1", "kind": "text", "x": 276, "y": 40, "anchor": "start", "text": "0.0095", "bold": true, "tone": "accent"},
    {"id": "p3", "kind": "text", "x": 276, "y": 160, "anchor": "start", "text": "0.0495", "bold": true, "tone": "mid"}
  ],
  "steps": [
    {"caption": "Start with the prior. Only 1 person in 100 has the disease D. The other 99 do not.",
     "show": ["root", "D", "N", "e1", "e2"], "draw": ["e1", "e2"], "highlight": ["e1"]},
    {"caption": "Now everyone is tested. A sick person tests positive 95% of the time. A healthy person tests positive 5% of the time (a false positive).",
     "show": ["Dp", "Dn", "Np", "Nn", "e3", "e4", "e5", "e6"], "draw": ["e3", "e4", "e5", "e6"], "highlight": ["e3", "e5"]},
    {"caption": "Multiply along a branch to get the chance of the whole path. Sick and positive: 0.01 x 0.95 = 0.0095.",
     "show": ["p1"], "highlight": ["e1", "e3", "D", "Dp", "p1"]},
    {"caption": "Healthy and positive: 0.99 x 0.05 = 0.0495. This is the bigger number, because healthy people are so many.",
     "show": ["p3"], "highlight": [{"id": "e2", "tone": "mid"}, {"id": "e5", "tone": "mid"}, {"id": "N", "tone": "mid"}, {"id": "Np", "tone": "mid"}, {"id": "p3", "tone": "mid"}]},
    {"caption": "We are told the test came back positive. So negative branches cannot have happened. Remove them. Only the two + paths remain.",
     "hide": ["Dn", "Nn", "e4", "e6"], "highlight": [{"id": "Dp"}, {"id": "Np", "tone": "mid"}]},
    {"caption": "Posterior = the sick-and-positive path divided by all positive paths. A positive test gives only about a 16% chance of disease.",
     "math": "$P(D\\mid +)=\\dfrac{0.0095}{0.0095+0.0495}\\approx 0.16$",
     "highlight": ["p1", {"id": "p3", "tone": "mid"}]}
  ]
}
